---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { href, REPO, toolCount, VERSION } from "../lib/docs";

const site = (Astro.site?.href ?? "").replace(/\/$/, "") + import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const win = `irm ${site}/install.ps1 | iex`;
const mac = `curl -fsSL ${site}/install.sh | bash`;
const tools = toolCount();
---
<Layout title="DaVinci Resolve MCP">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Edit in DaVinci Resolve by describing it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An MCP server that lets Claude, ChatGPT and other AI assistants drive DaVinci Resolve. It creates projects, imports
      media, builds and edits timelines, grades, mixes audio, adds titles and subtitles, and renders deliverables.
    </p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="#install">Install</a>
      <a class="btn" href={href("/docs/tools/")}>Browse {tools} tools</a>
      <a class="btn" href={REPO}>View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h">
    <h2 id="install-h">Install</h2>
    <div class="install">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Windows</h3>
        <p>Installs the server to <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\DaVinciResolveMCP</code> and registers it with your AI clients.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Press <kbd>Win</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd>, type <strong>powershell</strong> and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> (no admin needed).</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Copy</strong> below, then paste into PowerShell with a right-click or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>.</li>
          <li>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> and wait for it to finish.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="cmd"><code>{win}</code><button type="button" data-copy={win}>Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>macOS</h3>
        <p>Installs the server to <code>~/Library/Application Support/DaVinciResolveMCP</code> and registers it with your AI clients.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd>, type <strong>Terminal</strong> and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Copy</strong> below, then paste into Terminal with <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>.</li>
          <li>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> and wait for it to finish.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="cmd"><code>{mac}</code><button type="button" data-copy={mac}>Copy</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Configures every MCP client it finds: Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, VS Code (Copilot), Cline, Roo Code,
      Gemini CLI and Codex. Existing configs are merged, with a backup. Scripts: <a href={href("/install.ps1")}>install.ps1</a>,
      <a href={href("/install.sh")}>install.sh</a>. <a href={href("/docs/configuration/#mcp-clients-the-installers-configure")}>Details</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="card stack">
      <h3>After install</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Start <strong>DaVinci Resolve</strong> (Studio or free, 18.5 or later) and set <strong>Preferences → System → General → External scripting using</strong> to <strong>Local</strong>.</li>
        <li>Make sure 64-bit Python 3.6+ is on your PATH: the server talks to DaVinci Resolve through its official Python scripting API.</li>
        <li>Fully quit and reopen your MCP client, then ask: <em>"Check the DaVinci Resolve status, then create a 1080×1920 vertical timeline called 'Shorts'."</em></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="card stack">
      <h3>Manual install</h3>
      <p>Needs Git, Node.js 20+, pnpm (via Corepack) and 64-bit Python 3.6+.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Clone the repo: <code>git clone {REPO}.git</code>, then <code>cd DaVinci-Resolve-MCP</code>.</li>
        <li>Install and build: <code>corepack enable</code>, <code>pnpm install</code>, <code>pnpm build</code>.</li>
        <li>Register it with Claude Desktop: <code>scripts\install.ps1 -ConfigureClaude</code> on Windows or <code>./scripts/install.sh --configure-claude</code> on macOS.</li>
        <li>Check the setup: <code>scripts\diagnostics.ps1</code> or <code>./scripts/diagnostics.sh</code>.</li>
        <li>Then follow the <strong>After install</strong> steps above.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="note">Full guide, ChatGPT and remote HTTP: <a href={href("/docs/installation/")}>installation guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="what-h">
    <h2 id="what-h">What it does</h2>
    <div class="features">
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">{tools}</div><p>MCP tools: projects, media pool, timelines, editing, effects, speed, titles, subtitles, Fusion, color, Fairlight audio and rendering.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">Workflows</div><p>YouTube, social, documentary, cinematic and advertisement workflows plan a full edit you can dry-run and review before anything changes.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">Native</div><p>Everything is a real Resolve project, timeline and render job, not a flattened export, so you can keep editing by hand.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">Checked</div><p>Results come from DaVinci Resolve itself. Destructive actions need confirmation and a backup, and file access is limited to folders you allow.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <h2 id="how-h">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li>You ask your assistant for an edit.</li>
      <li>The server plans it and validates the arguments.</li>
      <li>DaVinci Resolve runs it through its official Python scripting API.</li>
      <li>The assistant inspects the timeline or render and revises.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Details: <a href={href("/docs/architecture/")}>architecture</a>, <a href={href("/docs/limitations/")}>limitations</a>. Current release: <a href={`${REPO}/releases/latest`}>v{VERSION}</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <script>
    for (const btn of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("button[data-copy]")) {
      btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.copy ?? "");
          btn.textContent = "Copied";
        } catch {
          btn.textContent = "Select it";
        }
        setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = "Copy"), 1600);
      });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
